common: fix fdt_for_each_subnode() argument order

The libfdt shipped in scripts/dtc uses the current upstream macro
signature:

  #define fdt_for_each_subnode(node, fdt, parent)

but most callers in this tree still use the pre-2018 U-Boot order with
the fdt blob first. lib/fdtdec.c was updated when libfdt was refreshed;
common/image-fit.c and common/image-sig.c were not, so they expand to

  for (fit = fdt_first_subnode(noffset, image_noffset); ...)

which assigns to the blob pointer and passes an int as the blob. That is
a real bug, not just a diagnostic: it was simply never exercised, because
GCC only warned about it until GCC 14 promoted -Wint-conversion to an
error and broke the tools build:

  common/image-fit.c:1014:35: error: passing argument 1 of
      'fdt_first_subnode' makes pointer from integer without a cast

Swap the first two arguments at the five call sites in common/ to match
the macro. The remaining old-order callers live in Tegra and Freescale
code that this board does not build.

Signed-off-by: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>

